# Summary
Introduced: admin-only control-plane auth configuration now creates an auth verifier, but the existing heartbeat path unconditionally enforces storage-node heartbeat authentication whenever any verifier exists.
The commit adds admin credentials as a reason to instantiate ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier, even when there are no storage-node credentials. However, RefreshNodeHeartbeat handling treats the mere presence of any auth verifier as a requirement to verify storage-node heartbeat auth. With an admin-only verifier, storage_node_credentials is empty, so signed heartbeats cannot match any node credential and plain heartbeats fail envelope decoding. The config validation only requires a cluster id for admin credentials; it does not require storage-node credentials. As a result, an operator enabling the new admin auth feature by itself can cause all storage-node leases to stop refreshing, leading to node expiry and service unavailability.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Admin-only control-plane auth configuration is accepted with a cluster id and no storage-node credentials.
- [x] Admin-only configuration/build path creates `Some(ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier)` with `storage_node_credentials.len() == 0` and `admin_credentials.len() == 1`.
- [x] `RefreshNodeHeartbeat` dispatch verifies heartbeat payloads whenever any verifier is present, not only when storage-node credentials exist.
- [x] A plain storage-node heartbeat sent through an admin-only verifier is rejected as missing auth and does not update the node lease.
- [x] A signed storage-node heartbeat sent through an admin-only verifier is rejected as UnknownCredential because the verifier has an empty storage-node credential map, and does not update the node lease.
## Report
Validated the finding at commit 491017af2bc8661f67a1e8267309b7b05d45d2f7. This is a Rust compiled project, but the bug is an availability/logic flaw rather than a memory-safety crash. Direct debug test reproduction was successful; Valgrind was attempted but unavailable (`bash: command not found: valgrind`); LLDB was used to trace the failing path.

Key code evidence: `crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:3177-3225` returns `Some(ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier)` whenever admin credentials exist and uses `ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier::new_empty(cluster_id)` when storage credentials are empty. `crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:5455-5468` shows `new_empty` creates an empty `storage_node_credentials` map. `crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:6465-6474` unconditionally calls `verify_storage_node_heartbeat_payload` for `RefreshNodeHeartbeat` whenever `auth_verifier` is `Some`. `crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:5819-5837` rejects plain heartbeat payloads as missing/malformed auth. `crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:5866-5876` rejects signed heartbeat envelopes when `storage_node_credentials` has no credential for that node. `crates/argmin-s3/src/config.rs:779-798` only requires a cluster id for admin credentials and does not require storage-node credentials.

Dynamic reproduction: I added two targeted unit tests in `crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs`. `admin_only_auth_verifier_rejects_plain_storage_node_heartbeat` constructs an admin-only verifier using `new_empty(...).with_admin_credentials(...)`, sends a normal `RefreshNodeHeartbeat`, and asserts rejection as Missing auth with lease deadline remaining `None`. `admin_only_auth_verifier_rejects_signed_storage_node_heartbeat_unknown_credential` sends a signed storage-node heartbeat to the same admin-only verifier and asserts rejection with `has no credential for node 1`, UnknownCredential metrics, and lease deadline still `None`. Command output: `cargo test -p storage 'admin_only_auth_verifier_rejects' -- --nocapture` -> `running 2 tests ... ok ... test result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed`.

The existing argmin-s3 test also confirms the new admin-only configuration builds a verifier with zero storage-node credentials: `cargo test -p argmin-s3 control_plane_unix_auth_verifier_includes_admin_credentials -- --nocapture` -> `test tests::control_plane_unix_auth_verifier_includes_admin_credentials ... ok`; that test asserts `status.storage_node_credentials().len() == 0` and `status.admin_credentials().len() == 1` at `crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:4451-4459`.

Debugger evidence: LLDB breakpoint at `control_plane.rs:5866` during the signed-heartbeat PoC stopped inside `ControlPlaneUnixAuthVerifier::verify_storage_node_heartbeat_payload`; backtrace showed the chain `verify_storage_node_heartbeat_payload` at `control_plane.rs:5866` <- `build_control_plane_unix_response_with_auth` at `control_plane.rs:6472` <- PoC test at `control_plane.rs:12946`. LLDB variable output showed `self->storage_node_credentials ... length = 0` and `heartbeat.node_id = 1`, confirming a signed heartbeat is rejected because the admin-only verifier contains no storage-node credential. This validates that enabling admin auth alone can prevent storage-node heartbeat lease refresh.

